1:["$","$Le",null,{"guide":{"slug":"first-aquarium-checklist","number":"02","category":"GETTING STARTED","title":"Your first freshwater aquarium checklist","intro":"Plan the aquarium around what you want to keep. Use this checklist to prepare a conversation with the shop before buying your equipment or livestock.","image":"/mas-aquarium-studio/aquarium.jpg","alt":"A freshwater planted aquarium photographed by Huy Phan","takeaway":"A filled tank is the beginning of setup. Water readiness comes before fish.","sections":[{"id":"plan","title":"Plan for the grown aquarium","body":"Check the adult size and compatibility of the fish you are considering. Tank size, filtration and temperature needs should follow that plan. Ask the shop to review the combination."},{"id":"equipment","title":"Check the essentials","body":"Prepare equipment suited to the aquarium and its intended inhabitants. Your setup list should include:","items":["An appropriately sized aquarium and filter.","Suitable lighting and a thermometer.","Temperature control if your chosen species need it.","Water conditioner, a suitable water test kit, a dedicated bucket and siphon."]},{"id":"water","title":"Prepare and test the water","body":"Use water conditioner according to its instructions. Check ammonia, nitrite, nitrate, pH and temperature. Establish biological filtration and discuss the results with the shop before adding fish."},{"id":"record","title":"Keep a simple setup record","body":"Write down the setup date, equipment and test results. Bring the record with your fish shortlist so the shop can help you assess the next step."}],"questions":["Is this equipment suitable for my planned fish?","Which water tests do I need?","What evidence will show that my filter is ready?"],"sources":[{"title":"RSPCA Australia — Aquarium water quality","url":"https://kb.rspca.org.au/categories/companion-animals/fish/why-is-water-quality-important-when-setting-up-a-fish-aquarium"},{"title":"RSPCA Australia — Tropical fish care","url":"https://kb.rspca.org.au/categories/companion-animals/fish/how-should-i-care-for-my-tropical-fish"}],"next":"before-fish-home","shopPlants":false}}]
